                    </summary>
                    <div class="premium-itinerary-content custom-blog-prose max-w-none">
                      <div class="bg-slate-50 p-4 rounded-md mb-6 border border-slate-200">
                        <p class="font-bold text-slate-800 mb-2">Stage Highlights:</p>
                        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-slate-700 m-0 space-y-1">
                          <li>Enjoy crispy, hot Vietnamese Banh Mi prepared by The Rice</li>
                          <li>Visit the traditional Dai Viet Cu Chi Lacquerware Village</li>
                          <li>Discover the secret trapdoors, underground wells, and the 200km tunnel system</li>
                          <li>Experience real tunnel crawling & test your skills at the sport shooting range</li>
                        </ul>
                      </div>

                      <p style="margin-bottom:14px"><strong>08:00 AM — Pickup at 195 De Tham, District 1:</strong> Depart from downtown Saigon in a private air-conditioned 7-seater van. During the 60-70 minute drive to the outskirts, you will enjoy a hot, crispy Vietnamese Banh Mi prepared by The Rice Travel Group's culinary team.</p>
                      
                      <p style="margin-bottom:14px"><strong>09:15 AM — Visit Dai Viet Cu Chi Lacquerware Village:</strong> Take a gentle stop at a traditional lacquer village. Witness artisans skillfully creating exquisite mother-of-pearl inlaid lacquer paintings, fine handicrafts, and gemstone jewelry.</p>
                      
                      <p style="margin-bottom:14px"><strong>10:00 AM — Explore the Cu Chi Tunnels Historical Site:</strong></p>
                      <ul style="list-style-type:disc; padding-left:20px; margin-bottom:14px;">
                        <li>Watch a historical documentary about the life and resilient fighting spirit of the Cu Chi troops and locals.</li>
                        <li>Discover subtly camouflaged secret trapdoors, underground water wells, subterranean meeting halls, and an intact wrecked American tank in the middle of the jungle.</li>
                        <li>Directly experience crawling through the underground tunnel layers, see termite-mound-simulated ventilation holes, and visit the weapon workshop making homemade arms from war scraps.</li>
                        <li>Test your marksmanship with AK-47 or M16 rifles at the shooting range (optional personal expense).</li>
                      </ul>

                      <div class="bg-amber-50 border-l-4 border-amber-500 p-4 my-4 rounded-r-md">
