                          <li>Enjoy a flavorful Southern-style lunch at a selected restaurant</li>
                          <li>Relax comfortably in the private 7-seater van back to HCMC center</li>
                        </ul>
                      </div>

                      <p style="margin-bottom:14px"><strong>12:00 PM — Enjoy Boiled Tapioca & Hot Cu Chi Tea:</strong> Gather under a rustic bamboo shelter in the Cu Chi forest to enjoy soft, fragrant boiled tapioca dipped in peanut-sesame salt — a dish closely associated with the resistance years, accompanied by a hot cup of jasmine tea.</p>
                      
                      <p style="margin-bottom:14px"><strong>12:30 PM — Specialty Lunch:</strong> The group enjoys a hearty lunch featuring Southern delicacies at a carefully selected, clean, and cool local restaurant.</p>
                      
                      <p style="margin-bottom:14px"><strong>01:30 PM — Depart back to downtown Saigon:</strong> The private 7-seater van drives you back to District 1 in a smooth, private, and air-conditioned environment.</p>
                    </div>
                  </details>

                  <!-- CHẶNG 3 -->
                  <details class="premium-itinerary-item">
                    <summary class="premium-itinerary-summary">
                      <div class="itinerary-toggle-icon"></div>
                      <span>Afternoon: Saigon Architectural Heritage Journey & Independence Palace</span>
                    </summary>
                    <div class="premium-itinerary-content custom-blog-prose max-w-none">
                      <div class="bg-slate-50 p-4 rounded-md mb-6 border border-slate-200">
                        <p class="font-bold text-slate-800 mb-2">Stage Highlights:</p>
                        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-slate-700 m-0 space-y-1">
                          <li>Admire the ancient French architecture of Notre Dame Cathedral & Central Post Office</li>
                          <li>Stroll along the peaceful Nguyen Van Binh Book Street</li>
                          <li>Visit Independence Palace — a heroic historical witness</li>
                          <li>Explore Ben Thanh Market and immerse in Saigon's vibrant rhythm</li>
                        </ul>
                      </div>

                      <p style="margin-bottom:14px"><strong>02:30 PM — Explore the Cultural & Architectural Heritage Complex of Downtown Saigon:</strong></p>
                      <ul style="list-style-type:disc; padding-left:20px; margin-bottom:14px;">
                        <li><strong>Notre Dame Cathedral & Central Post Office:</strong> A classic architectural masterpiece over 130 years old in the heart of the city featuring Gothic-Renaissance style.</li>
                        <li><strong>Nguyen Van Binh Book Street:</strong> A favorite shaded cultural rendezvous for locals and the youth of Saigon.</li>
                        <li><strong>Independence Palace:</strong> A historical mansion with unique architecture, preserving crucial historical transitional milestones of the nation.</li>
                        <li><strong>Ben Thanh Market:</strong> A long-standing trading icon packed with countless souvenirs and distinctive local specialties.</li>
                      </ul>

                      <div class="bg-sky-50 border-l-4 border-sky-500 p-4 my-4 rounded-r-md">
                        <p class="font-semibold text-sky-800 mb-1 flex items-center gap-2">
                          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor">
